{"id": "9th-u4-q086", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "factual", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "9th-tamil-u4", "lesson_id": "9th-tamil-u4-l3", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "uyir-vagai-classification", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "தொல்காப்பியர் கூற்றுப்படி 'மூன்றறிவு' கொண்ட உயிரினங்களுக்கு உரிய எடுத்துக்காட்டுகள் எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "சிப்பி, நத்தை", "B": "கரையான், எறும்பு", "C": "நண்டு, தும்பி", "D": "புல், மரம்"}, "explanation": "மூன்றறி வதுவே அதனொடு மூக்கே - தொடு உணர்வு, சுவைத்தல், நுகர்தல் ஆகிய மூன்று அறிவுகளைப் பெற்றுள்ள உயிரினங்கள் கரையான் மற்றும் எறும்பு ஆகும். சிப்பி, நத்தை - ஈரறிவு; நண்டு, தும்பி - நான்கறிவு; புல், மரம் - ஓரறிவு."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "According to Tholkappiyar, which creatures are categorized as possessing three senses (Moondrarivu: touch, taste, smell)?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Oyster, Snail", "B": "Termite, Ant", "C": "Crab, Dragonfly / Beetle", "D": "Grass, Tree"}, "explanation": "Termites and ants possess three senses (touch, taste, and smell). Oysters and snails have two senses; crabs and dragonflies have four; grass and trees have one sense."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", 